  "reveal": {
    "ledger_voiced": "From my book. The sitting ran as I ran it: the guttering of the lamp: a wick trimmed short at six o'clock; it wants ten minutes; the table's tilt: the wedge of my boot beneath the claw-foot; the spirit writing: the slates changed in the dark; chalk-crumb on my cuff; the cold draught: the window cord, loosed an inch before the lamps went out; the touch: a kid glove, stuffed with wool and kept on the ice; the scent of violets: a phial in my left sleeve; the right was held; the raps: my knee against the table's leaf, twice and thrice.\n\nAs to the evening's business: the account Xerxes Hartfield swore to was an invention, for those hands were out of the dark and about their own work. the Reverend Simeon Gaunt was past any sitting's reach before the lamps were lit.\n\nThe dead say what it profits me they say; on this occasion they profited Xerxes Hartfield more.",
